WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.250
- You have to sit next to
me and my coffee breath.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.480
You're welcome.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.313
Have y'all ever met?

00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:05.146
- No.
- No.

00:00:05.146 --> 00:00:06.433
- Okay.
- I'm excited.

00:00:06.433 --> 00:00:09.240
- I'm in awe, you're gorgeous.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.770
- [Kelly] We were talking about it.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.300
So wait, are you a superhero nerd like me?

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.377
- [Jonathan] Yeah, I'm like geeking out.

00:00:13.377 --> 00:00:14.400
- I'm so excited.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.840
I'm being real low key about it.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.097
- [Jonathan] Yeah, I'm
like, I need to get on you.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:18.630
I'm like really trying to hold it in.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.463
- I know.
- The Wasp right now.

00:00:19.463 --> 00:00:21.030
- Do you have anything you wanna ask?

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:21.863
- Yeah.

00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:22.946
Okay, so I didn't bring my notebook.

00:00:22.946 --> 00:00:23.779
- [Evangeline] I'm here for you.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:24.840
What do you need?
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.276
- So as I'm a big comic book fan.

00:00:27.276 --> 00:00:28.320
- All right.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.330
- [Jonathan] I've been reading
comic books since I was a kid

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.940
and a big thing for all of us nerds

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.259
is when characters constantly interact.

00:00:35.259 --> 00:00:36.390
- Yeah.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.310
- [Jonathan] For you, the Wasp,

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.480
you know, she's been with Ant-Man

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.690
but I would like to know if
you had to like do another film

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.523
with another random hero,

00:00:43.523 --> 00:00:45.960
team up with somebody
else and do that movie,

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.310
because that happens
all the time in comics--

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.180
- That's a great question.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.176
- [Jonathan] Who would you do it with?

00:00:50.176 --> 00:00:51.420
(Jonathan chuckles)

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.253
- [Kelly] Well, not it.

00:00:52.253 --> 00:00:53.086
(all laugh)

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.470
It could be it, or it
could just be the movie.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.303
- [Jonathan] Or the movie.

00:00:56.303 --> 00:00:57.136
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:57.136 --> 00:00:58.260
What's your choice? Yeah.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.835
- I'm gonna say that it'd
be really cool to do,

00:01:00.835 --> 00:01:03.810
even though normally
I'm really down on DC,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.890
I'm just gonna be honest here.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:05.723
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:05.723 --> 00:01:06.835
- Just really down on them.

00:01:06.835 --> 00:01:07.668
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:07.668 --> 00:01:11.178
- But like a Wonder Woman, Wasp crossover.

00:01:11.178 --> 00:01:12.270
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.890
- Where like, DC meets Marvel.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.137
- Wow, I don't know if
the world could take that.

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:17.040
- I can take it!
(audience laughs)

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.150
- It's a sick choice, okay.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:18.983
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:20.309
- Wouldn't you want to do
a movie with Wonder Woman?

00:01:20.309 --> 00:01:21.142
- [Jonathan] I mean...

00:01:21.142 --> 00:01:21.975
- Come on.

00:01:21.975 --> 00:01:22.808
Talk it out.

00:01:22.808 --> 00:01:23.671
- Do you just wanna be
in a scene with her?

00:01:23.671 --> 00:01:26.580
- If I could walk on set and say hi

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.930
and then like, walk off, I would do that.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.220
- [Kelly] I dunno if you'd want to, man.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.260
I met her one time and I was like...

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.440
I don't know that I've ever
felt inferior in my life,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.951
but I was like "Were we
supposed to come out like that?"

00:01:36.951 --> 00:01:39.060
- Like, I didn't get the memo to--

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.920
- Crazy tall Goddess vibes.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.045
I was like, "Okay."

00:01:42.045 --> 00:01:44.730
Anyway, what's going
on in this video, man?

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.810
I have to ask you.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:46.980
Here we go.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:47.850
What's happening here?

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.755
- [Jonathan] Oh, boy.

00:01:48.755 --> 00:01:49.713
(Jonathan chuckles)

00:01:49.713 --> 00:01:50.671
Oh yeah.

00:01:50.671 --> 00:01:51.588
And, and...

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:53.666
Yeah.

00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:54.499
There it goes.

00:01:54.499 --> 00:01:55.689
(audience gasps)

00:01:55.689 --> 00:01:56.772
- [Kelly] Like...

00:01:56.772 --> 00:02:01.230
What kind of superhuman
strength do you have?

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.610
You're just killing down walls.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.816
So wait, what happened?

00:02:03.816 --> 00:02:05.040
Were you dared?

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:05.940
- No.
(Jonathan chuckles)

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.880
So it was during filming of
season one of "Outer Banks"

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.820
and it's like me, Drew
Starkey, Austin North,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.770
we're kind of like doing
this, we're practicing stunts.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.390
And they had us in the
production office that day.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.223
- Yeah.

00:02:16.223 --> 00:02:17.610
- [Jonathan] And it used
to be like an old school

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.290
so they had like this little intercom

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.354
on the top in that video.

00:02:20.354 --> 00:02:22.500
There's a cup there, and we're like bored.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.090
Like we kind of like
gone through the stunt

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.020
and we're just kind of sitting there

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.090
waiting for the coordinator to get back.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:29.310
So we're like, "Let's have a dunk contest

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.630
with this little tennis ball."

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.463
- [Kelly] As you do.

00:02:31.463 --> 00:02:32.340
- As kids do.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.190
So I'm like "Let me Michael
Jordan this at the end,"

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.870
and there it goes.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.277
And I'm like, "oh no!"

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.600
And mind you, this is my
first season of a show period

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:43.530
doing anything.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.960
- [Kelly] So you're destroying
property right off the bat.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.793
- [Jonathan] Right,

00:02:46.793 --> 00:02:49.170
and so instead of like telling anybody,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.365
I just got outta there.

00:02:50.365 --> 00:02:51.648
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:51.648 --> 00:02:52.860
I skedaddled.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.120
So I get this like call
from our coordinator

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.400
and he likes to play jokes,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.668
so he's like, "Hey, JD,

00:03:01.668 --> 00:03:04.150
saw the hole in the production office.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.620
That's actually where like
microfiber wires were,

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.620
so all the WiFi's out
in the entire building

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.060
it's just gonna have to
come out of your check."

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.129
- I love him.

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:14.400
(audience laughs)

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.860
- This is my first money ever.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:16.693
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:03:16.693 --> 00:03:19.218
- I was like, "My check?"

00:03:19.218 --> 00:03:20.550
- Oh, that's so awesome.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.100
You always have such a good
time on set with everybody.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.450
Having done it now for a few seasons.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.030
Well, for those unfamiliar
with the "Outer Bank" series

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:27.973
tell everybody what it's about.

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:32.310
- Yeah, it's kind of like
adult Goonies almost,

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.143
where it's like--

00:03:33.143 --> 00:03:33.976
(Kelly gasps)
- I'm in.

00:03:33.976 --> 00:03:34.830
- Yeah.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:35.820
- [Jonathan] That's the elevator pitch.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.070
It's like these kids
who live on this island

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.180
or in the Outer Banks,

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.770
like right off the
coast of North Carolina.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:41.603
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:41.603 --> 00:03:44.520
- And that kid right
there with the open shirt

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.570
and the ponytail.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:46.403
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:46.403 --> 00:03:47.236
- [Jonathan] His dad goes missing.

00:03:47.236 --> 00:03:49.741
And so his friends, he's
looking for this treasure.

00:03:49.741 --> 00:03:51.840
So he gathers his friends together

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.190
and they go on this treasure hunt.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.440
There's mystery, romance,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:59.417
a lot of action and danger,
some chasing death, you know?

00:03:59.417 --> 00:04:00.750
- [Kelly] That's the best tease ever.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.680
- Yeah.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.350
It's a really like rabbit hole fun show.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.000
Like I always say, they
like to up the stakes

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:06.833
like every time.

00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.000
Every time you think it
can't get crazier, it does.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:09.840
- [Kelly] Gosh, I love it

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:10.974
- That reminds me of something.

00:04:10.974 --> 00:04:12.205
(Kelly chuckles)

00:04:12.205 --> 00:04:13.805
So weird, it sounds so familiar.

00:04:15.194 --> 00:04:16.279
- I love it.

00:04:16.279 --> 00:04:19.950
You said that you loved comic books before

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.650
but should we do a game
based on Marvel trivia?

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.060
How do you think you'd do?

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.715
- I mean like, is overqualified like a--

00:04:26.715 --> 00:04:27.892
(all laughs)

00:04:27.892 --> 00:04:29.350
- Oh my god, you're gonna kill me.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:30.510
- [Evengeline] I love it.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:33.456
- Okay, Outer Bank season
three premieres February 23rd

00:04:33.456 --> 00:04:34.623
on Netflix.

